          "heading": "what_we_did",
          "source_ids": [
            "sections.2",
            "sections.3"
          ],
          "text": "The team did blood tests, including a glucose check. These were normal. A toxicology screen was done and was negative. A CT scan of your head was done and was normal. No anti-seizure medicine was started. This is because it was a first seizure and the immediate risk of it happening again was low. The decision about anti-seizure medicine has been left for the neurology team after further tests."
